<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  VehicleBeastLabels.xml                    Jawa_Patches - new file 2026-08-20
  ============================================================================

  The four draught vehicles and the sled are drawn pulled by Tatooine beasts.
  Their HEALTH TAB still named the donor animals, so a player looking at a
  damaged sled read "Front Left Dog" over a picture of an eopie.

  This is the "separate, cheap job" NEOLITHIC_VEHICLE_BEAST_RESKIN_1 names.
  ⛔ LABELS ONLY. No texture work, no stat, no geometry, and nothing that
  changes what any vehicle does.

  The assignment is DECIDE's, ruled from measured baseBodySize, and the ladder
  is the point - do not swap one beast for another without redoing all of it:
      AV_DogSled          eopie   x2   bodySize 1.4
      AV_Chariot          dewback x1   bodySize 3.0
      AV_WarChariot       dewback x2   bodySize 3.0
      AV_OxCart           bantha  x2   bodySize 4.0
      AV_CoveredCarriage  ronto   x2   bodySize 6.0

  🔑 THE `label` IS PATCHED AND THE `key` IS NOT. `key` is the component's
  identifier - the vehicle's own code and its `tags` list address components by
  it - so renaming it would be a mechanical change wearing a cosmetic hat.
  `<tags><li>Dog</li></tags>` is likewise left alone for the same reason.

  ⚠️ THE SLED HAS FOUR COMPONENTS AND TWO EOPIES. The donor sled was pulled by
  four dogs and the art now shows a pair, but the component COUNT is structural
  health, not a headcount, and changing it is out of scope here. The four are
  named Front/Rear Left/Right Eopie, which reads correctly for a two-by-two
  team. Flagged to DECIDE rather than resolved quietly.

  ⏳ NOT DONE HERE - THE HURT SOUND. The sled's flesh type
  `AV_WoodenAndDogVehicle` points at SoundDef `AV_BulletImpact_Wood_And_Dogs`,
  whose grain list includes `Pawn/Animal/Dog/Dog_Injured`, so a shot sled still
  yelps like a dog. It is NOT patched here because the replacement path cannot
  be verified offline: vanilla ships its sounds inside Unity asset bundles, not
  as loose files, so no herbivore clip folder can be confirmed to exist from
  disk - and a wrong clip path is a silent no-sound. Filed separately.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Alpha Vehicles - Neolithic</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!-- AV_DogSled -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/Vehicles.VehicleDef[defName="AV_DogSled"]/components/li[key="FrontLeftDog"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>Front Left Eopie</label></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/Vehicles.VehicleDef[defName="AV_DogSled"]/components/li[key="FrontRightDog"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>Front Right Eopie</label></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/Vehicles.VehicleDef[defName="AV_DogSled"]/components/li[key="RearLeftDog"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>Rear Left Eopie</label></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/Vehicles.VehicleDef[defName="AV_DogSled"]/components/li[key="RearRightDog"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>Rear Right Eopie</label></value>
        </li>

        <!-- AV_Chariot -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/Vehicles.VehicleDef[defName="AV_Chariot"]/components/li[key="Horse"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>Dewback</label></value>
        </li>

        <!-- AV_WarChariot -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/Vehicles.VehicleDef[defName="AV_WarChariot"]/components/li[key="LeftHorse"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>Left Dewback</label></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/Vehicles.VehicleDef[defName="AV_WarChariot"]/components/li[key="RightHorse"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>Right Dewback</label></value>
        </li>

        <!-- AV_OxCart -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/Vehicles.VehicleDef[defName="AV_OxCart"]/components/li[key="LeftOx"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>Left Bantha</label></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/Vehicles.VehicleDef[defName="AV_OxCart"]/components/li[key="RightOx"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>Right Bantha</label></value>
        </li>

        <!-- AV_CoveredCarriage -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/Vehicles.VehicleDef[defName="AV_CoveredCarriage"]/components/li[key="LeftHorse"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>Left Ronto</label></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/Vehicles.VehicleDef[defName="AV_CoveredCarriage"]/components/li[key="RightHorse"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>Right Ronto</label></value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
